  "scope": "CkUI admission generations and weak layer-membership observer, with native and actual AngelScript consumer cases in real second-player CommonUI Pause PIE, plus twelve compatible authoring checks.",
  "capabilities": [
    "Rejected observation is atomic and retryable; successful observation or explicit Stop is terminal.",
    "Cover/uncover retains the same admission; committed removal/clear/auto-deactivation, resource reset, layout replacement and same-frame inherited remove/re-push invalidate it.",
    "Actual production class-pool reuse receives a new admission generation.",
    "Retirement is one-shot and deferred through CoreTicker; query is synchronous and callback-free, and the ticker works while the world is paused.",
    "Exact weak player/controller/world/layout/layer/root identities reject foreign-controller reassignment.",
    "Watcher does not retain owner and weak callbacks/ticker do not retain watcher; last external root is dropped during callback GC and callback-created replacement remains independent.",
    "Native ProcessEvent uses discovered parameter properties; actual AngelScript invokes TryObserve/queries/Stop and receives OnRetired with exact retired identity."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The real Pause menu remains native; the script probe is a UObject consumer, not a migrated screen.",
    "The watcher does not release authored sessions, acquire/release pause, restore focus or remove widgets; consumer policy remains separate.",
    "Retirement is deferred, not an immediate committed-removal notification; pure queries must gate work during the deferred interval.",
    "The focused fixture uses zero-duration stack transitions; nonzero animated transitions are not directly tested.",
    "Same-player controller replacement, cross-world travel and uint64 generation exhaustion are inspected contracts without direct runtime cases.",
    "Blueprint-callable/pure/assignable reflection metadata is checked, but actual Widget Blueprint VM execution is not exercised.",
    "Physical gamepad behavior, packaged builds and loose-file packaged lookup remain unverified.",
    "The real second-player widget layer overlays a single scene view; two-view split-screen rendering remains outside this proof."
  ]
}
